1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:00,750
Points.

2
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:05,550
The only thing clans love more than drops, and arguing about drops.

3
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:13,550
Every task is worth some points.

4
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:17,550
When a team finishes it, the team gets those points.

5
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:17,950
Simple.

6
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:22,350
What's less simple is who on the team gets the credit.

7
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:25,150
Points are split by contribution.

8
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:29,950
If two of you each got half of a five point task,

9
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:32,750
you each get two and a half.

10
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:37,550
So yes, the person who carried the team gets to prove it,

11
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:38,350
with decimals.

12
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:40,350
Bingo adds bonuses.

13
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:45,550
Finish a row, a column, or a diagonal and your team gets line

14
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:46,750
points on top.

15
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:49,950
Fill the whole board for the blackout bonus.

16
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:54,750
Empty cells are free spaces, already done for everyone, as a treat.

17
00:00:55,550 --> 00:01:00,750
Filter the board by team to see exactly who's close to a line,

18
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:04,350
and who's one Vorkath kill away from a breakdown.

19
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:07,950
Standings update live, here and in Discord.

20
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:11,550
The Discord leaderboard is one message, edited in place,

21
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:15,550
so your channel doesn't turn into a wall of scoreboards.

22
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:18,350
Every point has a receipt.

23
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:23,150
The completion history shows who pulled what, for which team, and when.

24
00:01:23,150 --> 00:01:27,950
It is very useful for settling arguments, and for starting new ones.

25
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:29,950
Then there's effort.

26
00:01:29,950 --> 00:01:33,550
Hours spent on things that actually move the board,

27
00:01:33,550 --> 00:01:37,550
not hours spent five-manning a boss that isn't on it.

28
00:01:37,550 --> 00:01:39,950
Busy isn't the same as helpful.

29
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:43,550
When it ends, you can pay out.

30
00:01:43,550 --> 00:01:47,950
The prize pot tracks buy-ins and donations, but it's advertised only.

31
00:01:47,950 --> 00:01:51,950
No real gold moves, you still trade it in game.

32
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:55,150
Clan points go out for placement and participation.

33
00:01:55,150 --> 00:02:00,350
And by default, the person who signed up and went AFK on the

34
00:02:00,350 --> 00:02:01,950
winning team gets nothing.

35
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:02,350
Justice.

36
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:02,750
Finally.

37
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:05,550
That's the core of it.

38
00:02:05,550 --> 00:02:10,750
Next up, the fancier formats: loot sweeps, skill and boss of the week,

39
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:15,950
the board game, and Conquest, where your clan fights over a map of

40
00:02:15,950 --> 00:02:16,350
Gielinor.

41
00:02:16,350 --> 00:02:17,150
Bring snacks.
